    "market_inefficiency": "When price closes beyond the 20-bar Donchian boundary (prev_high20/prev_low20) with elevated volume, resting stop liquidity beyond the range is consumed in a short cascade. With higher-timeframe slope aligned, that cascade tends to continue rather than immediately mean-revert, creating a temporary directional dislocation larger than round-trip friction.",
